There was some discussion of the kicking bug.  I just got a
segmentation fault by kicking a sink.  I typed 25^Dhh.  The first time
I kicked the sink and the second time I got the seg fault.  There were
some black pudding corpses piled nearby and a succubus wandering
around.  Good thing I copied my save file.  Until the program
stabilizes, why not add a checkpointing feature.  I understand that on
some machines save files are protected.

